    "layers": {
      "type": "ces-stat-proof",
      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "",
        "heading": "Your Skin Has 5 Layers. Everything You Have Tried Only Reached The First One.",
        "subheading": "",
        "body": "<p>Here is the thing none of those products will tell you. They all stopped at the same place. The surface of your skin. Eye bags don't live there.</p><p>Eye bags don't start at the surface. They start deeper — in the tissue where fluid builds overnight, where skin gets thinner with age, where the hollow that makes you look tired actually forms.</p><p>Creams sit on top. Serums sit on top. Even the gel patches you have already tried sit on top.</p><p>Your skin is designed to keep things out and it is very good at its job. That is not a quality problem with the products you chose. It is a physics problem. Nothing applied to the surface can cross that barrier.</p><p>That is the only reason nothing has worked. Not because you did not try hard enough. Because everything stopped at the same wall.</p>",
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/6_2.webp",
        "image_position": "beside_body",
