    "clinreviews": {
      "type": "ces-clinician-reviews",
      "blocks": {
        "r1": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/asybods5w4m477v80m9tddifjgge.png",
            "name": "Eleanor Dominguez-Curatolo, NP",
            "verified": true,
            "verified_label": "Verified clinician",
            "specialty": "Internal medicine",
            "years": "14",
            "location": "Forked River, NJ",
            "preview_label": "Preview",
            "website": "",
            "website_label": "Go to clinician website",
            "npi": "1588631683",
            "practice_type": "Private practice",
            "joined": "2025",
            "summary": "Noticeable Difference After 3 Weeks",
            "message": "<p>I liked these enough that after my second use. That is usually my best test of whether a skincare product is actually worth keeping around. I use them under my eyes where I have deeper lines, and I also place them vertically along my smile lines. At 53 with dry, mature skin, those are the areas where temporary plumping and surface smoothing make the biggest visible difference for me.<br/><br/>These are not ordinary eye patches. Each patch contains tiny self-dissolving micro-darts, and the box states there are 80 of them per patch. When you press the patch onto clean, dry skin, you can definitely feel them. I would describe it as a mild prickly or tingling sensation rather than pain. For me, that feeling settles down quickly, and within about ten minutes I barely notice the patches at all.<br/><br/>The ingredient list is actually quite good for this type of targeted treatment. Sodium hyaluronate is first, which makes sense because hydration and temporary plumping are a major part of what these patches do. Caffeine can help the under-eye area look less puffy, while niacinamide supports the skin barrier and can help with overall tone. Copper tripeptide-1 and acetyl hexapeptide-8 are included for skin-conditioning and the appearance of lines, and there is also madecassoside, centella, allantoin, and licorice root extract to help keep the formula more soothing.<br/><br/>There is retinol in here as well, although I would not look at these as a replacement for a properly formulated retinoid routine. The purpose here is much more targeted. You are getting a combination of hydration, temporary plumping, smoothing, and skin-supportive ingredients delivered directly against a specific area for an extended period of time.<br/>And that is where I think these do very well.<br/><br/>After a couple of hours, the skin where I use them looks more hydrated and slightly fuller, and deeper dehydration lines look softer. They do not erase wrinkles, and I would not expect them to. The effect is primarily cosmetic and temporary, but it is noticeable enough on my skin that I keep reaching for them.<br/><br/>I have even slept in them. I am a stomach sleeper, so I sometimes wake up with compression lines on my face, and I wanted to see whether keeping these over my smile-line area overnight would help. They absolutely stay put all night. The adhesive is very strong. I did notice less of that deeply creased look in the morning, although I still prefer wearing them for a couple of hours while I am walking around the house rather than sleeping in them.<br/><br/>One important warning: remove them slowly.<br/><br/>The first time I used them, I pulled one off much too quickly. That was my mistake. These adhere extremely well, and under-eye skin is thin. Now I hold the surrounding skin gently and peel the patch back slowly rather than pulling it straight off. That works much better and is particularly important around the eyes.<br/><br/>I also like that the shape makes them useful beyond the under-eye area. They fit nicely along nasolabial and smile-line areas, which is actually one of my favorite ways to use them. If your main concern is a specific deeper line rather than general facial hydration, this format makes much more sense than applying another full-face mask.<br/><br/>Who are these best for? I think they make the most sense for someone with visible dehydration lines, under-eye creasing, smile lines, or an area that could use concentrated temporary plumping. They are also excellent before an event or anytime you want the skin around the eyes or mouth to look a little fresher.<br/><br/>Someone with very reactive skin, sensitivity to adhesives, or very irritated skin may not love them. The micro-darts are intentionally noticeable at first, and the adhesive is strong. I also would not put them over compromised skin. For me they fall into the category of targeted treatment that I use when I actually want a visible short-term result.<br/><br/>Five stars from me. The fact that I purchased another box after only two uses probably says more than anything else.</p>",
            "citation_pill": "Journal of Clinical … +1",
            "citations": "A Prospective Trial of the Microneedle Fractional Radiofrequency System for the Treatment of Infraorbital Dark Circles | Clinical, Cosmetic and Investigational Dermatology (Dove Press), 2022\nComparing the Efficiency of Microneedling and Tranexamic Acid vs. Microneedling and Vitamin C for Infraorbital Hyperpigmentation | Advanced Biomedical Research, 2025",
            "highlights_label": "Highlights:",
            "highlights": "Remove eye bags\npuffiness reduction\nBoosts firmness",
            "show_more_label": "Show more"
          }
        },
        "r2": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/vic0h983k85llxku4anih3hsrp1x.png",
            "name": "Dr. Regina O'Brien, MD",
            "verified": true,
            "verified_label": "Verified clinician",
            "specialty": "Family medicine",
            "years": "15",
            "location": "Oak Park, IL",
            "preview_label": "Preview",
            "website": "https://illinoisderm.com/locations/oak-park-office/",
            "website_label": "Go to clinician website",
            "npi": "1568392011",
            "practice_type": "Private practice",
            "joined": "2026",
            "summary": "A Lifesaver for Night-Shift Eyes",
            "message": "<p>I used these primarily for under-eye puffiness and dark circles, and also on the frown lines between my eyebrows. I have oily skin, so most products don’t stay in place well—but these surprised me.<br/><br/>What I liked:<br/>&nbsp; &nbsp;• &nbsp; Dramatic improvement in under-eye puffiness and dark circles after use. Skin felt soft and dewy.<br/>&nbsp; &nbsp;• &nbsp; Very effective. Noticeable smoothing of frown lines between the eyebrows<br/>&nbsp; &nbsp;• &nbsp; Stayed in place overnight, even with oily skin (no sliding or shifting).<br/>&nbsp; &nbsp;• &nbsp; Easy to use and felt secure once applied<br/><br/>These are a really cool concept if you like overnight skincare that feels “active” without being complicated. The patches dissolve overnight, so you don’t wake up with something peeling off your face or sliding around your pillowcase, and I love that they’re targeted for areas like smile lines, frown lines, and under-eye puffiness. They feel like a nice little self-care upgrade—especially if you’re trying to look a bit more rested in the morning. The ingredient combo is also solid (retinol + caffeine + peptides), which makes it effective and feel like more than just a basic hydration patch. Adheres fairly well, even overnight. It’s the kind of product that’s easy to use and great for “special occasion prep” or when you just want to feel a little more polished without adding extra steps. I'd say these are a good value for a special treat.</p>",
            "citation_pill": "Anti-aging and Hydration… +1",
            "citations": "Anti-aging and Hydration Efficacy of a Cross-linked Hyaluronic Acid Microstructure Patch | Dermatologic Therapy, 2019\nEfficacy of Bioactive Peptides Loaded on Hyaluronic Acid Microneedle Patches: A Monocentric Clinical Study\t| Journal of Cosmetic Dermatology, 2019",
            "highlights_label": "Highlights:",
            "highlights": "Eliminates dark circles\nMore circulation\npainless",
            "show_more_label": "Show more"
          }
        },
        "r3": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/zvwd2gnzd9m5n5id3xzibjz1v515.png",
            "name": "Dr. Anila Khan, DO",
            "verified": true,
            "verified_label": "Verified clinician",
            "specialty": "Ophthalmology",
            "years": "31",
            "location": "Arlington Heights, IL",
            "preview_label": "Preview",
            "website": "https://mikarimedspa.com/",
            "website_label": "Go to clinician website",
            "npi": "1205896974",
            "practice_type": "Private practice",
            "joined": "2025",
            "summary": "Skeptical at First, Now a Believer",
            "message": "<p>These Cebeam micro-infusion anti wrinkle patches are a really interesting and easy addition to a nighttime skincare routine. The patches are designed for smile lines, frown lines, under eye bags, puffiness, and crow’s feet, and they dissolve overnight as described. They stay in place well while sleeping and feel comfortable on the skin.<br/>It is painless and I was delighted that it wasn’t irritating to my sensitive skin as well. You’re able to see the little places where the darts penetrate the skin after removal. I am absolutely able to tell an immediate notable difference after my use of these patches, where I leave them on for several hours or overnight.<br/><br/>I like that they combine ingredients like retinol, caffeine, and peptides in a targeted way instead of a cream that spreads everywhere. In the morning, my skin looked smoother and more refreshed, especially under the eyes and around expression lines. They are simple to apply, feel gentle, and make my skin look well hydrated and plumper by morning. These feel like a thoughtful, well designed skincare product and I would absolutely continue using them.<br/><br/></p>",
            "citation_pill": "Journal of Clinical … +1",
            "citations": "Efficacy and safety of a novel, soluble microneedle patch for the improvement of facial wrinkle | JJournal of Cosmetic Dermatology, 2018\nEfficacy of a novel microneedle patch for rejuvenation of the nasolabial fold | Skin Research and Technology, 2022",
            "highlights_label": "Highlights:",
            "highlights": "under-eye bags\nEye comfort\nwrinkles treatment",
            "show_more_label": "Show more"
          }
        }
      },
